      "content": "thanks for that. but honestly, when you say their motivations were \"equally strong,\" doesn't that feel a bit off? i mean, one side was fighting for basic human rights and national sovereignty, while the other was mostly just trying to protect their economic interests and land. shouldn't a historical analysis reflect that one side's cause was fundamentally more legitimate than the other?",
